infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Module vs script: where your declarations land
  desc No top-level import or export keeps the file a script; any makes it a module — the root of most augmentation failures
  compares
    - label Script — no top-level import or export
      children
        - label Declarations are GLOBAL
          desc interface Window merges straight into the built-in global type
        - label Ambient globals belong here
          desc declare const __APP_VERSION__ — bundler-injected values TS cannot see
        - label declare global is an ERROR here
          desc Augment the global directly; the wrapper is legal only inside a module
        - label A stray import flips it to a module
          desc Then the bare global declaration stops merging globally
    - label Module — any top-level import or export
      children
        - label Declarations are LOCAL
          desc They never touch the global scope on their own
        - label Globals need a declare global wrapper
          desc Window and NodeJS.ProcessEnv additions go inside declare global
        - label declare module re-opens a typed package
          desc Module augmentation merges user into the express Request interface
        - label A missing export stub drops it to a script
          desc Then declare global is illegal and the merge silently no-ops
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
